    "name": "The 20s Breakout",
    "family": "breakout",
    "entry_long": "close > donchian_high_prev(high,0.0) + 0.0 * (donchian_high_prev(high,0.2) - donchian_low_prev(low,1))",
    "exit_long": "close < donchian_low_prev(low,1) - 0.2 * (donchian_high_prev(high,1) - donchian_low_prev(low,1))",
    "stop_loss_pct": null,
    "take_profit_pct": null,
    "notes": "The documented Ratio 0.2 is applied to the previous bar's range, so a close beyond the prior high plus 20% of that range is the upside breakout and the mirrored band is the exit, which subsumes the LevelPoints confirmation. SignalBar 1 is inherent in next-bar execution, and 1000/2000-point protection, Mode selection and the long/short permission switches are order features."
